From dd242cbe37127b8c41248d3b25ade8a34072a9c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahmadsb101 <ahmadsb101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:45:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] frp: free-running pipelines time each write from its own
 iteration; read stage and RTL depths

Replaces the read-after-write +1 rule. From Vitis 2023.2 cosim waveforms:
- issue: an FRP pipeline issues only when each input FIFO holds the reads it
  has requested plus this one, so an item read at stage r must be there r
  cycles earlier (read-after-write + r, r from the RTL read condition);
- depths: Vitis can enlarge FIFOs (pragma 2 -> RTL 5); the RTL depth is used;
- no freeze: a missing input only holds back the next issue. The fifo write
  carries anchor_delta (write stage - the iteration's last read stage) and goes
  on its own node, timed from that read's stage, with its write-after-read stall
  on that node only; the module ends after its last FRP writes.

30 microbenchmarks (1/3/7 inputs, depth 2/16, slow producer/consumer, II 2,
two FRP stages, conditional reads) and the small SODA set: 0 or one mapping
step (-8/-9 cycles) against cosim; heat3d/jacobi3d residual +126..+153 -> 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
